    {
      "id": 56208,
      "name": "Cosmonaut Zero",
      "username": "Cosmonaut_Zero",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/cosmonaut_zero/{size}/2520_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-03-21T17:21:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"tacticaltechkyle\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/d2c977/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> tacticaltechkyle:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>dypaca wrote:</b><br><blockquote>I believe the ruling for Combat Stance in this old thread: <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/combat-stance-0\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/combat-stance-0</a>&nbsp;was that it goes off for each target each turn.Personally, I always found the other reading (goes off once per turn total) to be much more intuitive though.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nThe wording of Combat Stance and Miss Infos card are very different. They are not compareable.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The only real difference is \"is dealt\" vs. \"deals.\" The important part for this discussion, the part that determines which targets trigger the effect, is the same. The version on Miss Information is still ambiguous sans ruling, but it's less unclear than the other versions. I am 100% certain that the ruling applies here.</p>\n<p>I agree the wording is not good if that's the intent, but I also think the ruling unambiguously applies here. This is another thing like \"would/instead,\" where a single additional word (an extra \"each\" in this case) would make it a lot clearer.</p>",
      "post_number": 8,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:31:10.582Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
